. It also supports object-oriented applications by treating all files as objects with user-defined and system-defined attributes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85711">NTFS file system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1571040">NTFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1297_85711_1968693"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An advanced file system designed for use specifically with the Windows NT operating system. It supports long filenames, full security access control, file system recovery, extremely large storage media, and various features for the Windows NT POSIX subsystem. It also supports object-oriented applications by treating all files as objects with user-defined and system-defined attributes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85711">NTFS file system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968693">sistema de fitxers NTFS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12979_1135479_1968855"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual display of data in a dashboard that can be coordinated with other report views by using filters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1135479">report</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun<