tronic instance of one-to-many schemas. Usually documents are sent between two processes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="258949">document</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2915616">missatge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14412_318308_2915616"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An electronic instance of one-to-many schemas. Usually documents are sent between two processes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318308">message</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2915616">missatge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14423_232843_1970419"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Paragraph formatting you can use to assign a hierarchical level (Level 1 through Level 9) to paragraphs in your document. For example, after you assign outline levels, you can work with the document in outline view or in the Document Map.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232843">outline level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970419">nivell d'esquema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage"