ular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17516_648980_1970238"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A process by which you evaluate a probable outcome based on three scenarios: best-case, expected-case, and worst-case.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648980">Program, Evaluation and Review Technique analysis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970238">anàlisi d'Avaluació de programes i tècnica de revisió</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17519_648986_1970239"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that indicates how much of the task's budget should have been spent, given the actual duration of the task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648986">BCWP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970239">CPFR</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17519_648986_1970240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that indicates how much of the task's budget should have been spent, given the actual duration of the task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648986">BCWP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970240">cost pressupostat de la faena realitzada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17519_648987_1970239"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that indicates how much of the task's budget should have been spent, given the actual duration of the task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648987">budgeted cost of work performed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970239">CPFR</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17519_648987_1970240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that indicates how much of the task's budget should have been spent, given the actual duration of the task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648987">budgeted cost of work performed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970240">cost pressupostat de la faena realitzada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17520_648988_1970241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that shows how much of the budget should have been spent, in view of the baseline cost of the task, assignment, or resource. BCWS is calculated as the cumulative time-phased baseline costs up to the status date or today's date.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648988">budgeted cost of work scheduled</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970241">cost pressupostat de la faena planificada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17520_648988_1970242"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that shows how much of the budget should have been spent, in view of the baseline cost of the task, assignment, or resource. BCWS is calculated as the cumulative time-phased baseline costs up to the status date or today's date.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648988">budgeted cost of work scheduled</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970242">CPFP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17520_648989_1970241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that shows how much of the budget should have been spent, in view of the baseline cost of the task, assignment, or resource. BCWS is calculated as the cumulative time-phased baseline costs up to the status date or today's date.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648989">BCWS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970241">cost pressupostat de la faena planificada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17520_648989_1970242"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The earned value field that shows how much of the budget should have been spent, in view of the baseline cost of the task, assignment, or resource. BCWS is calculated as the cumulative time-phased baseline costs up to the status date or today's date.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="648989">BCWS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970242">CPFP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17525_649087_1967779"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A number from 0 to 1 that reveals how closely the estimated values for the trendline correspond to your actual data. A trendline is most reliable when its R-squared value is at or near 1.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="649087">coefficient of determination</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967779">coeficient de determinació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17525_649087_1967780"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A number from 0 to 1 that reveals how closely the estimated values for the trendline correspond to your actual data. A trendline is most reliable when its R-squared value is at or near 1.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="649087">coefficient of determination</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967780">valor R quadrat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17525_649088_1967779"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A number from 0 to 1 that reveals how closely the estimated values for the trendline correspond to your actual data. A trendline is most reliable when its R-squared value is at or near 1.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="649088">R-squared value</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967779">coeficient de determinació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote>