rials through the pipelines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162890">P&amp;ID</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970667">diagrama de canonades i instruments</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24863_1166063_1970665"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A diagram that shows how industrial process equipment is interconnected by a system of pipelines, including instruments and valves that monitor and control the flow of materials through the pipelines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166063">piping and instrumentation diagram</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970665">P&amp;ID</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24863_1166063_1970667"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A diagram that shows how industrial process equipment is interconnected by a system of pipelines, including instruments and valves that monitor and control the flow of materials through the pipelines.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1166063">piping and instrumentation diagram</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970667">diagrama de canonades i instruments</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24868_1162904_1967802"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The portion of data distribution that is determined to be more or less than some critical value. For example, the far left and far right areas of a bell curve.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162904">tail</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967802">cua</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24869_1162906_1967804"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A test in which the null hypothesis is rejected if the value of the test statistic falls into either tail of the probability distribution (i.e. is either less than a first critical value or greater than a second critical value).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162906">two-tailed test</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967804">prova doble</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24869_1176836_1967804"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A test in which the null hypothesis is rejected if the value of the test statistic falls into either tail of the probability distribution (i.e. is either less than a first critical value or greater than a second critical value).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1176836">two-sided test</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967804">prova doble</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2488_235380_1968867"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A paper or electronic request made to the purchasing department to acquire a specified amount of goods or services from external suppliers and vendors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235380">purchase requisition</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968867">sol·licitud de compra</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24880_1162958_1970666"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A stencil in the Shapes window that shows all the Quick Shapes from the Quick Shapes area of each open stencil.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1162958">Quick Shapes stencil</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970666">plantilla de formes ràpides</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2490_1050717_1566712"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reusable magnetic storage medium. The floppy disk used today is the rigid 3.5-inch microfloppy that holds 1.44 MB. It is called floppy because the first varieties were housed in bendable jackets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1050717">magnetic disk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1566712">disquet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2490_1470_1566712"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reusable magnetic storage medium. The floppy disk used today is the rigid 3.5-inch microfloppy that holds 1.44 MB. It is called floppy because the first varieties were housed in bendable jackets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1470">floppy disk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1566712">disquet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2490_339962_1566712"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A reusable magnetic storage medium. The floppy disk used today is the rigid 3.5-inch microfloppy that holds 1.44 MB. It is called floppy because the first varieties were housed in bendable jackets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="339962">disk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1566712">disquet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24903_1165764_1571263"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An option that isolates the foreground portion of an image and make the background transparent.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165764">Remove Background</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1571263">Suprimeix el fons</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="24919_1165832_1969387"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A slider control where the maximum and minimum values of the range can be modified.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165832">multi-stop slider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></la