roperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2489809">Timesheet</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42645_2415869_2418053"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The context menu that pops up when text is selected in the Researcher panel giving the option of adding the selected text only or adding the selected text and a citation for the text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2415869">Add Cite</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2418053">Afig una citació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4265_101189_1770796"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database repository for information about a computer's configuration. The registry contains information that Windows continually references during operation, such as: profiles for each user; the programs installed on the computer and the types of documents that each can create; property settings for folders and program icons; what hardware exists on the system; which ports are being used. The registry is organized hierarchically as a tree, and it is made up of keys and their subkeys, hives, and entries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="101189">registry</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770796">registre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4265_1167347_1770796"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database repository for information about a computer's configuration. The registry contains information that Windows continually references during operation, such as: profiles for each user; the programs installed on the computer and the types of documents that each can create; property settings for folders and program icons; what hardware exists on the system; which ports are being used. The registry is organized hierarchically as a tree, and it is made up of keys and their subkeys, hives, and entries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1167347">system registry</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770796">registre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42654_2417345_3110013"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool for erasing markings on a 2D surface.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2417345">eraser</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3110013">esborrador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42660_2418366_2420342"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that puts together a PowerPoint or Sway outline based on the user's query, giving him or her a set of options to choose from, as well as advice on what can be included in the presentation or the sway.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2418366">QuickStarter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2420342">Inici ràpid</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42661_2418994_2419966"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device, such as a PC, some tablets, a 2-in-1, or an All-in-one, that uses the traditional Win32 app model and typically make use of COM or .NET runtime.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2418994">desktop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419966">dispositiu d'escriptori</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42661_2419397_2419966"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device, such as a PC, some tablets, a 2-in-1, or an All-in-one, that uses the traditional Win32 app model and typically make use of COM or .NET runtime.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419397">desktop device</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419966">dispositiu d'escriptori</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42664_2419020_2419967"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A business rule that provides explicit, mandatory criteria to use when making a decision or taking action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419020">policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419967">norma</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42666_2419437_2420340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The web tool which allows users to try Microsoft Graph REST API requests and see the responses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2419437">Graph explorer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2420340">Explorador del Graph</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpee