ctivity, set screen time limits, check on a child's location, limit which websites and games they can access, and require approval to purchase from the Microsoft Store.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956707">family group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2997046">grup familiar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52730_2956708_2997093"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that searches through on-premises file shares and SharePoint document libraries and folders for sensitive items that meet the criteria of a data loss prevention policy.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956708">scanner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2997093">explorador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52731_2956709_2997042"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To calculate the derivative, or rate of change, or a function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956709">differentiate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2997042">diferenciar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52732_2956710_2997036"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To multiply on the left by one element and on the right by its inverse.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956710">conjugate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2997036">conjugar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52733_2956711_2997086"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Denoting different kinds of mutual relation, often with reference to the substitution of reciprocals for given quantities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956711">reciprocal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2997086">recíproc</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52734_2956714_2997066"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To subject to the operation of finding the integral of a function.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956714">Integrate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNot