ty (minus distributed income, such as dividends) since its start date or inception.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="415801">retained earnings</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1969218">benefici no distribuït</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="859_616474_1969218"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The accumulated earnings of a company or entity (minus distributed income, such as dividends) since its start date or inception.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616474">retained profit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1969218">benefici no distribuït</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8595_269326_3001216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The proprietary protocol to provide remote display and input capabilities over network connections for Windows-based applications between two computers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269326">Remote Desktop Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3001216">RDP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8595_269326_3001217"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The proprietary protocol to provide remote display and input capabilities over network connections for Windows-based applications between two computers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269326">Remote Desktop Protocol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3001217">Protocol d'escriptori remot</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8595_269327_3001216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The proprietary protocol to provide remote display and input capabilities over network connections for Windows-based applications between two computers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269327">RDP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3001216">RDP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8595_269327_3001217"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The proprietary protocol to provide remote display and input capabilities over network connections for Windows-based applications between two computers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269327">RDP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3001217">Protocol d'escriptori remot</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8609_2856023_2572517"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any of a family of processes that software developers use to minimize risk by developing applications incrementally, over a series of short iterations. In this model, real-time communications, such as in person conversations and telephone calls, are preferred over written documentation; the primary measure of progress is working software, instead of hours spent, tasks completed, documents reviewed, or phases signed-off; stakeholders are expected to collaborate, instead of negotiating; and planning happens continuously in order to respond to change.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2856023">Agile methodology</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2572517">mètode àgil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8609_460694_2572517"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any of a family of processes that software developers use to minimize risk by developing applications incrementally, over a series of short iterations. In this model, real-time communications, such as in person conversations and telephone calls, are preferred over written documentation; the primary measure of progress is working software, instead of hours spent, tasks completed, documents reviewed, or phases signed-off; stakeholders are expected to collaborate, instead of negotiating; and planning happens continuously in order to respond to change.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="460694">Agile method</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2572517">mètode àgil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="862_1098947_1967595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software program that uses Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) for its core communication protocol and that delivers Web-based information to the user in the Hypertext Markup Language (HTML) language.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1098947">web-based application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967595">aplicació web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="862_131917_1967595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software program that uses Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) for its core communication protocol and that delivers Web-based information to the user in the Hypertext Markup Language (HTML) language.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="131917">Web application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967595">aplicació web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="862_131918_1967595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software program that uses Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) for its core communication protocol and that delivers Web-based information to the user in the Hypertext Markup Language (HTML) language.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="131918">web-enabled application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967595">aplicació web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="862_637226_1967595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software program that uses Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) for its core communication protocol and that delivers Web-based information to the user in the Hypertext Markup Language (HTML) language.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="637226">Web-based application</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967595">aplicació web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8639_20909_1969884"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Content or links that an administrator associates with specific keywords, and that are displayed prominently in search results when a query contains one of those keywords.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="20909">Best Bet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1969884">opció més probable</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8641_184378_2932054"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The permission setting that permits a person or domain to add the user to contact lists, see the user's status, or send instant messages to the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184378">Allow</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2932054">Permís</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8645_145897_1968739"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A predesigned, generic web page you can use to create new custom pages. Some of the page templates in FrontPage provide typical page content, while others provide common page layouts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145897">Page template</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968739">plantilla de pàgina</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8657_2140019_1563753"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The person in charge of managing a computer. The administrator is responsible for installing software, assigning passwords, and managing files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2140019">admin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1563753">administrador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8657_318135_1563753"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The person in charge of managing a computer. The administrator is responsible for installing software, assigning passwords, and managing files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318135">computer administrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1563753">administrador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8657_9827_1563753"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The person in charge of managing a computer. The administrator is responsible for installing software, assigning passwords, and managing files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="9827">administrator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1563753">administrador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8664_55395_1770260"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The stylistic attributes of a font — such as bold, italic, and underline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="55395">font style</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1770260">estil de lletra</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8667_185906_1968145"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An instant message conversation in which one or both participants is broadcasting a video feed by using a camera.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="185906">video conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968145">conversa de vídeo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="867_418629_1968275"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To take action to deflect a phone call after the phone rings but before the call is answered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="418629">redirect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968275">redirigir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="869_557910_1967989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An optional Microsoft Exchange 2000 Server component that is installed on a designated server in an administrative group. It provides centralized administration and archival of private keys, and maintains every user s private encryption key in an encrypted database. The keys are used for encrypting email messages and signing messages with digital signatures.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="557910">Key Management Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967989">Servei d'administració de claus</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8696_183901_1968396"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A slide template that defines default formatting or the position of placeholders for one or more slides in a presentation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="183901">content master</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968396">patró de contingut</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8698_237284_1970804"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An operating unit whose managers are accountable for budgeted and actual expenditures.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237284">cost center</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970804">centre de costs</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8702_168246_1968126"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A meeting participant who cannot initiate desktop or application sharing or presenting and whose permissions are controlled by the organizer and presenters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="168246">attendee</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968126">assistent</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8706_186134_1571143"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of rules on a computer and a portable device that allow digital media files and other information to be synchronized.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186134">partnership</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1571143">associació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8714_186176_1968366"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A context menu that enables the user to preview the contents of a file with the Office Preview Handler (OPH) in Outlook (either documents attached to email or SharePoint documents in Outlook).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="186176">PowerPoint Previewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968366">Visualitzador previ del PowerPoint</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8732_137331_1970121"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Adds preset visual effects to text on slides. Ranging from subtle to exciting, each scheme usually includes an effect for the slide title and an effect that is applied to bullets or paragraphs on a slide.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="137331">animation scheme</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1970121">combinació d'animació</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8741_187466_1968489"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a UML Static Structure or UML Component diagram, one of two types of interfaces that can be connected to class or component shapes and has a lollipop shape.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="187466">lollipop interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968489">interfície de piruleta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8744_35474_1967601"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A standard system control that initiates a command.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="35474">command button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967601">botó d'orde</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8744_35475_1967601"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A standard system control that initiates a command.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="35475">push button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1967601">botó d'orde</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8747_351591_1571190"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature in Windows that allows users to access and manage printers, multi-function printers, digital cameras and scanners.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="351591">Printing and Imaging Devices</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1571190">Dispositius d'impressió i de processament d'imatges</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8751_418607_1588618"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To prevent another user from initiating a conversation and from viewing your presence or other information, such as your personal information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="418607">block</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1588618">bloquejar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8752_178607_1968765"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A discussion with a customer or colleague.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="178607">conversation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968765">conversa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8757_558600_1968350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The list of answers to a search request that match the search criteria specified by the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="558600">search results</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968350">resultats de la recerca</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8763_335523_1968908"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An item such as an appointment, business note, email message, file, or task that is linked to an Account, Business Contact, Opportunity, or Business Project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="335523">communication history item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968908">element d'historial de comunicacions</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8770_361568_1968944"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service that exposes access to LOB data sources</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="361568">line-of-business service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968944">servei de línia de negoci</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8770_361569_1968944"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A service that exposes access to LOB data sources</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="361569">LOB service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968944">servei de línia de negoci</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8776_370830_1968968"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A listing or document selected as the best recommendation in the Site Directory.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="370830">Spotlight Site</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968968">lloc de Serveis en línia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8780_100131_1571246"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The temporary storage place on Windows where deleted files are transferred and remain until manually emptied and files are permanently deleted, which allows users to retrieve files until that point.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="100131">Recycle Bin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1571246">Paperera de reciclatge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8783_413984_1969010"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Baseline data that apply throughout a business or to a financial model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="413984">assumption</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1969010">hipòtesi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8789_252130_1968890"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables the user to access information from an accounting system from within Business Contact Manager for Outlook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="252130">Accounting Integration</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ca-ES-valencia"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1968890">Integració de la comptabilitat</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8790_232417_1967984"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of domain names and email addresses that you want to receive messages from. E-mail addresses in Contacts and in the Global Address Book are included in this list by default. People you sent messages to will be added to the list.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232417">Safe Senders List</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet